Cursor Prompt — Fix PWA vs Browser Waitlist State Persistence

Context

We have a mobile-first web app + PWA onboarding flow with:

Intro screens

Waitlist email submission

Confirmation screen

Early Access / Community Mode screen

Currently, when a user:

Enters the onboarding in the browser

Submits their email to the waitlist

Installs the PWA

…the app forgets that the user already submitted their email and shows the waitlist again.

This is incorrect UX.

Goal

Ensure that users who already submitted their email on the same device:

Never see the waitlist screen again

Automatically re-enter Early Access after PWA install

Are not required to re-enter their email unless they explicitly reset

Email confirmation (double opt-in) must NOT block Early Access.

Required Fix (Authoritative)
1. Introduce a local onboarding state (device-level)

Create a persistent local state that survives:

Browser refresh

PWA install

App reopen

Use localStorage (or IndexedDB if already used elsewhere).

Key name

ummahflow_onboarding


Shape

interface OnboardingState {
  email: string
  waitlistSubmitted: boolean
  earlyAccessUnlocked: boolean
  submittedAt: string // ISO timestamp
}

2. Write to local state immediately after waitlist success

When the waitlist API returns success (email accepted):

localStorage.setItem(
  "ummahflow_onboarding",
  JSON.stringify({
    email,
    waitlistSubmitted: true,
    earlyAccessUnlocked: true,
    submittedAt: new Date().toISOString()
  })
)


This must happen:

BEFORE showing the “You’re on the list” screen

WITHOUT waiting for email confirmation

3. App bootstrap logic (browser + PWA)

On every app load (including PWA start), run this logic:

const onboarding = localStorage.getItem("ummahflow_onboarding")

if (onboarding?.waitlistSubmitted === true) {
  // user already joined waitlist on this device
  skipIntroAndWaitlist()
  showEarlyAccess()
} else {
  showIntroOnboarding()
}


Important

Do NOT rely on backend session or cookies for this

Local device state is the source of truth for onboarding flow

4. Email confirmation behavior

Email confirmation is backend-only and must not block UI access.

Rules:

User can access Early Access immediately after submitting email

Confirmation email is required only for:

Launch access

Notifications

UI should optionally show a reminder text:

“Bitte bestätige deine E-Mail, damit wir dich benachrichtigen können.”

Do NOT:

Block Early Access

Re-show waitlist

Force re-entry of email

5. Edge cases (intentional behavior)
Scenario	Expected behavior
User clears browser storage	Waitlist shown again
User switches device	Waitlist shown
User opens PWA after install	Early Access shown
User reloads page	Early Access shown
User not confirmed email	Early Access still shown

This is correct and intentional.

6. Optional (but recommended): helper hook

Create a helper:

useOnboardingState()


Exposes:

{
  hasJoinedWaitlist: boolean
  email: string | null
  unlockEarlyAccess: () => void
  resetOnboarding: () => void
}


Use this hook everywhere onboarding logic is needed.

Acceptance Criteria (Must Pass)

User submits email in browser → installs PWA → sees Early Access, NOT waitlist

No second email input required on same device

Early Access available without email confirmation

Clearing storage resets flow

Works on iOS Safari + installed PWA

Non-Goals (Do NOT implement)

❌ Forcing login or authentication

❌ Blocking Early Access behind email confirmation

❌ Using cookies instead of persistent storage

❌ Asking for email twice on same device

Build exactly this behavior. Do not improvise UX logic.